# Mana Crypt: each Crypt has its own upkeep trigger, so two of them put two coin flips on the stack in Bot1's upkeep (and none
# in Bot2's), and the mana abilities add {C}{C} each, {C}{C}{C}{C} in all. (A coin flip is not a die roll, so a [Dice] section
# cannot fix it: what the flip does to Bot1's life is not asserted, only that two triggers wait on the stack.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mana Crypt
Mana Crypt
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Crypt.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Crypt#2.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {C}{C}{C}{C}
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Triggers(Mana Crypt; Mana Crypt)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mana Crypt; Mana Crypt
